## 📌 GraphQL Request Format
APA requires an **array** of operations:
[
  {
    "operationName": "ViewerQuery",
    "variables": {},
    "query": "query ViewerQuery { viewer { id __typename ... } }"
  }
]
Copilot should always generate this format.

### GraphQlRequest.cs
```csharp
public class GraphQlRequest
{
    public string OperationName { get; set; }
    public string Query { get; set; }
    public object Variables { get; set; }
}
```

### GraphQlResponse.cs
```csharp
public class GraphQlResponse<T>
{
    public T Data { get; set; }
    public GraphQlError[] Errors { get; set; }
}
```

### 📌 ApaClient.cs Requirements
Copilot should generate an APA client with:
```csharp
public class ApaClient
{
    private readonly HttpClient _http;

    public string AccessToken { get; set; }

    public ApaClient(HttpClient http)
    {
        _http = http;
    }

    public Task<T> SendAsync<T>(string query, object variables);
    public Task<T[]> SendBatchAsync<T>(IEnumerable<GraphQlRequest> requests);
}
```

### Behavior Rules
- Always attach the Authorization header.
- Always send an array of GraphQlRequest.
- Always deserialize into GraphQlResponse<T>[].

### 📌 Starter Query (Viewer)
Copilot should use this as the default test query:
```
query ViewerQuery {
  viewer {
    id
    __typename
    ... on Member {
      firstName
      lastName
      emailAddress
      leagues(current: true) {
        id
        name
        slug
      }
    }
  }
}
